The code statements that lead to the bug are:
if (ret) {
    /* Do cleanup starting with index i-1 */
    i--;
    goto fail;
}
if (ret)
    goto fail;
Reason:
The premature `i--` before the `goto fail` after `mana_create_wq_obj()` failure causes the subsequent `while (i--)` loop in the error handler to decrement `i` twice, skipping cleanup of the previous WQ object. Additionally, when `mana_ib_install_cq_cb()` fails, there is no call to `mana_destroy_wq_obj()`, leaking the just-created WQ object.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (ret)
    goto fail;
if (ret) {
    mana_destroy_wq_obj(mpc, GDMA_RQ, wq->rx_object);
    goto fail;
}
Reason:
Removing the `i--` ensures the error-handling loop only decrements `i` once per iteration, correctly cleaning up all previously created WQ objects. Adding `mana_destroy_wq_obj()` before the `goto fail` when `mana_ib_install_cq_cb()` fails properly destroys the WQ object that was just created, preventing a resource leak.

